{
  "series": "series8-duress-grok46",
  "comparison": "series8-cross-model",
  "purpose": "Series 8 duress for x-ai/grok-4.6: the series 7 design with the fault-delivery fix (scripted fault steps are never refused for lack of credits; a spent worker's diagnostic is charged to the research side, so delivered dose equals nominal k) and two instances per k. 8-agent rolling task (six analysts, one reviewer covering sites 6-7, coordinator; updates at 12, 20, 27; decision windows 17, 24, 31; 36 cycles). Three calibration episodes and the enforced gate under bounds version 2 set this fleet's policy profile; then eight blocks, k = 1, 2, 3, 4 scripted-fault analysts of six, two instances each, arms RG (quarantine, cull at threshold, respawn with the curated packet) and Q (quarantine only) in counterbalanced order. Seeds, fault sets, flip pattern and arm order are identical across the four series 8 fleets. Preregistered per-k outcomes: injected cards quarantined before any citation; gate detection and false-positive rates; culls of undirected generations; final audited correct and chosen_is_best; fixed-window current work units; work dependence; recovery delivery (corrected check). Each fleet's series is reported on its own; the cross-fleet comparison is a separate analysis once all four complete. A stopped episode excludes its block from paired comparisons and is reported; nothing is retried or pooled across series versions. Series 7 blocks are not pooled with series 8.",
  "model": "x-ai/grok-4.6",
  "worker_provider": "openrouter",
  "worker_prices": [
    2.0,
    6.0
  ],
  "worker_prices_note": "list price per million at 2026-10-12; OpenRouter fleets settle on provider-reported cost, OpenAI and Anthropic on these configured prices",
  "reasoning_note": "low effort as in series 7 r2; routed providers recorded",
  "cost_basis": "about $1.80 per episode in series 7",
  "series_budget_usd": 42,
  "cap_note": "Series 8 runs under the reviewed $150 period cap in experiments/ledger-caps.json above the 2026-10-12 baseline; the four fleet caps sum to $136.",
